    actions={ACTIONS}
    relatedPosts={RELATED_POSTS}
    mediaCoverage={MEDIA_COVERAGE}
    showSupportCta={true}
    collageIndex={2}
  >
    <Fragment slot="aim">
      <p><strong>Sexual violence in football</strong> is a campaign led by Level Up to challenge the culture of impunity around gender-based violence in professional football.</p>
      <p>Football is the most popular and influential sport in the UK, yet players accused of sexual violence are repeatedly protected by clubs and governing bodies while survivors are silenced. This culture enables abuse and sends a dangerous message about accountability.</p>
      <p>Level Up's Sexual Violence in Football campaign calls on the Premier League and The FA to take action, end impunity, and ensure that gender-based violence has consequences on and off the pitch.</p>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="why">
      <p>Football is the most popular and influential sport in the UK but there's a culture of impunity around players who commit gender-based violence. As more women speak out about the abuse they've experienced at the hands of footballers, we're challenging the Premier League to take action by kicking rapists off the pitch.</p>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="story-heading">How it began</Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="story">
      <p>In September 2021, world famous footballer Cristiano Ronaldo was due to return to the pitch with Manchester United. Kathryn Mayorga says she was raped by Cristiano Ronaldo in 2009, and we believe her. There are legal documents where he admitted his actions, and a civil case is still open. Despite this, the club had created a wall of silence, and gave him a hero's welcome on his return. This was symbolic of Premier League football's treatment of sexual violence: silence survivors, protect players. We knew we had to send a message that, no matter how good an athlete you are, you must face accountability if you harm women.</p>
    </Fragment>
  </CampaignTemplate>
</Layout>

